-- name: Verify passed but no test touched alongside source
-- class: Consistency
-- metric: alignment_collect_d2
-- action: add or update tests alongside the source changes that shipped, or fix the project's verify command if it does not actually exercise tests
-- severity: WARN
-- guardrail: BOTH SIDES OF THIS DISAGREEMENT LIVE IN alignment-collect's OWN d2 RECORD -- spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-30-loopsmith-insight-data-platform-design.md:529's own parenthetical names alignment-collect d2 tests_touched_with_source_pct directly; alignment-collect.sh's own printf (lines 448-449) emits tests_touched_with_source_pct and test_command_known together in one object, so no join is needed or possible. ROUND-2 POST-PR-REVIEW BLOCKING FIX (PR #203, second pass): the prior round's json_type(raw_payload,'$.dimensions.d2')='OBJECT' guard protected only the d2 CONTAINER's own shape, never the SIBLING SCALAR fields read out of a container that genuinely IS an object -- a d2 that is a real object but whose own tests_touched_with_source_pct or test_command_known is itself a nested JSON object/array/string was UNGUARDED, and a bare CAST(json_extract(...) AS INTEGER/BOOLEAN) RAISES DuckDB's ConversionException on a real type mismatch (COALESCE only catches a NULL result, never an exception) -- reproduced live: {"dimensions":{"d1":{"commits_with_source":{"x":1}},"d2":{...}}} crashed evaluate_rule entirely, hiding every well-formed row sharing that scan. FIXED IN TWO LAYERS. LAYER 1, UNCONDITIONAL CRASH-SAFETY: every extraction of tests_touched_with_source_pct, test_command_known, and commits_with_source now uses TRY_CAST, never bare CAST -- TRY_CAST returns SQL NULL for ANY conversion failure instead of raising, confirmed live for every malformed shape tried (object, array, string, bool cross-casts) against every target type this rule uses. This closes the crash at its root, independent of guard presence, ordering, or DuckDB's own AND-evaluation strategy -- CONFIRMED LIVE, POST-PR-REVIEW, THAT A json_type GUARD ALONE DOES NOT RELIABLY PREVENT THIS CLASS OF CRASH: a minimal two-line reproduction (`WHERE json_type(x)='BOOLEAN' AND CAST(x AS BOOLEAN) IS TRUE` against a row whose x is a malformed object) STILL RAISED, proving DuckDB does not always short-circuit AND on a guard's own FALSE result before evaluating a later expression referencing the same field -- TRY_CAST is not a redundant belt-and-suspenders measure here, it is the ONLY mechanism this rule relies on for crash-safety. LAYER 2, PER-FIELD json_type GUARDS, IN BOTH POPULATION AND EVIDENCE, FOR A DIFFERENT REASON -- TRY_CAST IS PERMISSIVE, NOT MERELY SAFE: TRY_CAST(... AS INTEGER) also coerces a numeric STRING ("5") or a JSON BOOLEAN to a real integer; TRY_CAST(... AS BOOLEAN) also coerces a JSON INTEGER (1/0) or a bool-parseable STRING ("true") to a real boolean -- confirmed live. Without the type guard, a wrong-shaped-but-coercible value (e.g. tests_touched_with_source_pct: "0", or test_command_known: 1) that population correctly excludes (json_type mismatch) would still LEAK into the evidence query's own output as a false, confirmed finding -- reproduced live, mutation-tested: with only the evidence-side test_command_known guard removed, a mixed store (one well-formed pack, one with test_command_known: 1) returned population=1 (correct) but TWO evidence rows, the second one a wrong-shaped value silently coerced into a false WARN. This is WORSE than a crash (a confidently wrong answer, not a loud failure), and it is why json_type(...) IN ('UBIGINT','BIGINT')/= 'BOOLEAN' remains in the evidence WHERE for tests_touched_with_source_pct and test_command_known even though TRY_CAST alone already prevents any exception -- mutation-tested per field (see the test file's own coercion-leak tests), each one's removal caught by exactly one dedicated test. commits_with_source's OWN GUARD IS DELIBERATELY SOFTER -- `json_type(...) IS NULL OR json_type(...) IN ('UBIGINT','BIGINT')` -- NOT a bare IN(...): commits_with_source is a SECONDARY, existence-only gate here (not this rule's own measured dimension, which is test_command_known/tests_touched_with_source_pct), and a payload with a well-formed d2 but NO d1 AT ALL is an explicitly OUT-OF-SCOPE, PRE-EXISTING, UNREACHABLE-VIA-THE-REAL-WRITER case (named so, not fixed, by this round's own review) that must keep rendering PASS via COALESCE(...,0)-softening, not flip to ABSENT as a side effect of this round's crash-safety work -- the IS NULL branch specifically preserves that outcome for a MISSING commits_with_source while the second branch still excludes a PRESENT-but-wrong-typed one (ABSENT), pinned by test_a_wellformed_d2_with_no_d1_at_all_is_pass_not_absent alongside test_commits_with_source_shaped_as_an_object_is_absent_not_a_crash. THE TOP-LEVEL d2='OBJECT' CONTAINER CHECK IS GONE, NOT MERELY UNUSED -- RE-DERIVED, NOT ASSUMED: with the per-field guards above in place, a d2 that is itself null/array/scalar makes the dotted path into tests_touched_with_source_pct/test_command_known resolve to SQL NULL (confirmed live: json path traversal through a non-object parent returns NULL, never raises), which already fails both per-field IN/= guards -- the container check added no additional exclusion once the per-field guards existed, confirmed by mutation (reverting it to the round-1 shape while the per-field guards stayed in place caught nothing), so it was deleted rather than kept as unexplained cruft. FIRES ONLY ON ZERO TOUCHED TESTS (tests_touched_with_source_pct = 0), NEVER A PERCENTAGE CUTOFF -- an existence/emptiness comparison against 0, matching coverage_gate_absent.sql's/coverage_degraded_collector.sql's own established idiom, deliberately not a tuned magnitude. REQUIRES commits_with_source > 0 SO A TRIVIAL 0% IS NEVER MISREAD AS A REAL DISAGREEMENT -- alignment-collect.sh only computes tests_pct nonzero when COMMITS_WITH_SOURCE > 0 (line 396); a window with zero source commits emits tests_touched_with_source_pct: 0 trivially, and this rule must not fire on that. test_command_known IS TRUE, NEVER IS NOT FALSE -- a payload missing the key entirely, or shaped wrong, extracts NULL/is excluded upstream by its own json_type guard, and NULL IS TRUE is FALSE regardless (three-valued logic, Design decision 5); with this round's guard, a d2 that is a well-formed object but omits test_command_known entirely now ALSO renders ABSENT, not PASS, at population -- the round-1 "unreachable via the real writer" nit this superseded is resolved as a side effect, not a regression: alignment-collect.sh always emits test_command_known whenever it emits d2 at all, so this changes no real behavior, only a synthetic-payload edge case. MALFORMED-PAYLOAD DISCLOSURE, RE-SCOPED AGAIN THIS ROUND: SYNTACTICALLY INVALID JSON (raw_payload is non-NULL text that will not parse as JSON at all) still makes every json_extract/json_type call in this rule's population and evidence queries raise DuckDB's InvalidInputException -- TRY_CAST does not protect against this, because the exception is raised by json_extract/json_type themselves parsing the raw text, before any CAST/TRY_CAST ever runs; this fails LOUD, not silent, so it is not spec:534's forbidden collapse, and it is the identical, unguarded pattern every one of the six already-shipped rules (and metrics 5/20/24/41) shares against the same raw_payload column -- widening scope to guard against syntactically-invalid JSON across the catalog is out of this story's scope (see .sdlc/plans/120.md Risks). VALID JSON OF THE WRONG SHAPE, AT ANY FIELD THIS RULE READS, now renders ABSENT (or, for a missing-but-not-malformed commits_with_source specifically, the out-of-scope PASS), never a crash and never a silent false PASS. ORDER BY'S TOTAL-ORDER CLAIM, CORRECTED (LOW finding, post-PR-review round 2): `rowid` is deterministic WITHIN A SINGLE QUERY EXECUTION against an append-only table -- it is NOT a persistent row identity across executions once any DELETE has occurred (a delete followed by a CHECKPOINT can renumber a surviving row's own rowid, DuckDB's own documented physical-storage-position semantics, verified by an independent reviewer) -- no DELETE FROM fact_collector_pack exists under insight/ today, so this ordering guarantee holds in practice, but the claim here is scoped to exactly that: one query's own result-set ordering is deterministic, not a durable identity fact_collector_pack itself carries (it has no primary key, and collected_ts alone is not unique either) -- the same disclosed limitation coverage_degraded_collector.sql's own ORDER BY carries, closed here for THIS rule's own evidence rows only. A NOTE ON json_type OF A JSON NULL LITERAL, VERIFIED LIVE AGAIN THIS ROUND, BYTE-FOR-BYTE, AGAINST THE EXACT TWO-ARGUMENT FORM THIS RULE USES (`json_type(raw_payload, path)`, duckdb 1.4.5): it returns the four-character STRING 'NULL' (Python `str`, `IS NULL` evaluates to FALSE for it), distinguishable from a genuinely missing key, which returns actual SQL NULL (Python `None`, `IS NULL` evaluates to TRUE) -- reconfirmed directly before writing this sentence; this does not change any guard's own behavior (both outcomes correctly fail every `= 'X'`/`IN (...)` comparison here either way), but the specific factual claim is restated here, with its own verification command, precisely because a prior review round asserted the opposite of what this session's own live check shows.
-- population: SELECT count(*) FROM fact_collector_pack WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1' AND (json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') IS NULL OR json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') IN ('UBIGINT', 'BIGINT')) AND json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') IN ('UBIGINT', 'BIGINT') AND json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') = 'BOOLEAN'
SELECT
    project_id,
    collected_ts,
    TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER) AS commits_with_source,
    TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') AS INTEGER) AS tests_touched_with_source_pct,
    TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') AS BOOLEAN) AS test_command_known
FROM fact_collector_pack
WHERE schema = 'alignment-collect/v1'
  AND (json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') IS NULL
       OR json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') IN ('UBIGINT', 'BIGINT'))
  AND json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') IN ('UBIGINT', 'BIGINT')
  AND json_type(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') = 'BOOLEAN'
  AND TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.test_command_known') AS BOOLEAN) IS TRUE
  AND COALESCE(TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d1.commits_with_source') AS INTEGER), 0) > 0
  AND TRY_CAST(json_extract(raw_payload, '$.dimensions.d2.tests_touched_with_source_pct') AS INTEGER) = 0
ORDER BY project_id, collected_ts, rowid
